 "hypothesis": "H79-A (CTHM-PoE) + H79-B (SGMC-Coulomb): (1) Four zero-topography crustal-thermomechanical & hydrothermal alteration operators (H79_aniso_conduit_plume, H79_demag_argillic_crest, H79_euler_contact_index, H79_grav_mt_gouge_juxtapose) plus strike-aligned USGS SGMC lithologic-contact Coulomb reactivation (H79_sgmc_coulomb_react) detect Neogene-Quaternary faults concealed beneath Great Basin playas and bajadas; (2) Factoring blind inference into two physically orthogonal HGB experts (56-col zero-topography M_crustal x 26-col morphometric M_morpho) via floor-protected log-odds Product-of-Experts stops Family B scarp features from starving blind crustal splits at shallow tree depths.",
 "mechanism": "1) Strain-oriented anisotropic spring/vent hydrothermal plume log-density along principal extensional fault azimuth theta_f = 0.5*atan2(-e_xy, 0.5*(e_xx - e_yy)). 2) Magnetite-destruction argillic alteration crest combining thorium-normalized K excess (K - Th regression residual) with RTP magnetic-low trough along regional gravity gradients. 3) 3D potential-field Euler structural-index contact selector isolating steep fault steps (SI in [0, 1]) from deeper spheres/plutons (SI >= 2). 4) Gravity horizontal-gradient x shallow MT electrical conductivity gouge juxtaposition. 5) Strike-aligned SGMC contact proximity weighted by Kreemer strain rate and 2-m temperature excess. Shipped LOQO artifact uses the 56-column zero-topography M_crustal_sgmc expert to satisfy both external_sparse <= 70% and own_lineage <= 70% simultaneously.",
